   304	> **PROPOSITION BI-4 (charged vs branch-exchanged, all `N`).** Fix
   305	> `p ∈ Sing A_F` with `r_p` branches, and let `T_p := ∪_l h_l^{-1}(eta^{-1}(p))`
   306	> be the points of the dicriticals over `p`. Then, in the contracted model:
   307	> ```text
   308	>   sum_{t ∈ T_p}  sum_{branches Gamma of Ē_X at t}  deg(Phi|_Gamma)
   309	>          =  r_p ( a - a_p )  =  r_p [ (r_p-1) W + K_p ] ,
   310	>   of which  <=  K_p = sum_{t ∈ T_p} k_t  is SAME-BRANCH (Phi(Gamma) = b(t)),
   311	>   the remainder being BRANCH-EXCHANGED.
   312	> ```
   313	> At a unibranch `p` (`r_p = 1`) there is no exchange and the inequality is an
   314	> equality: `K_p = a - a_p` is carried entirely, and only, by the same-branch
   315	> branches. At a `p` with `K_p = 0` every branch of `Ē_X` at every `t ∈ T_p` is
   316	> exchanged.
   317	>
   318	> *Proof.* Each of the `r_p` punctures `P_b` of `A_F~-bar` over `p` carries, by
   319	> BE Prop 3.1, places of `E` at infinity of total degree `a - a_p`; the `r_p`
   320	> puncture-fibres are disjoint, giving `r_p(a - a_p)` in total; in the
   321	> contracted model each such place converges to a point of `T_p` and is a branch
   322	> `Gamma` of `Ē_X` there with `deg(Phi|_Gamma)` its degree over `A_F-bar`. The
   323	> same-branch bound is `E-CHARGE` summed over `t ∈ T_p`. ∎
