xmodel/b3-boundary-instrument-review-grok46-20260902.md:145:A unit lift (`m=n=1`) has transfer factor `n/Deg=1` (DF-4), so source branch determinants equal the target ones. Two unit lifts merging over `det B>1` repeat a non-unit determinant, contradicting DF-7. With DF-6 (`det R_{v_0}=1`, `det D,L>1`) such merges are confined to the `R`-side. This is the mechanism DR uses (DR:379, 391, 448). "Coprimality kills are kills of the multiplicity of `E`'s sheets" is accurate for unit-lift merges; it does not claim every coprimality kill in Lemmas 8–9 is about `E`.
