    89	## 1. MF-EXACT
    90	
    91	Take a generic target coordinate pair `(u,v)` and a generic affine line
    92	`L={u=gamma}`. Equivalently
    93	
    94	```text
    95	C_L = F^{-1}(L) = { alpha P + beta Q = gamma },
    96	```
    97	
    98	with `(alpha,beta)` and `gamma` outside the usual finite bad set. This is the
    99	generic member of the affine pencil generated by `P,Q`.
   100	
   101	Since `Jac F` is a nonzero constant, `dF` is an isomorphism everywhere. For
   102	generic nonzero `du`, `d(u o F)=du o dF` never vanishes. Thus `C_L` is smooth
   103	and reduced. The degree of `C_L` as an affine plane curve is
   104	`D_F=max(deg P,deg Q)` after choosing `(alpha,beta)` so that the top terms do
   105	not cancel.
   106	
   107	The restriction over `L\A_F` is the degree-`N` etale cover
   108	
   109	```text
   110	C_L \ F^{-1}(A_F) -> L \ A_F .
   111	```
   112	
   113	Zariski's generic-line theorem gives the surjection used in DG:317-320 and
   114	DR:216-219, so the restricted cover has transitive monodromy. Therefore the
   115	open curve is connected, and the smooth curve `C_L` is connected and
   116	irreducible. Let `X_L` be the smooth projective model and let
   117	`pi:X_L -> P^1` be the compactified map induced by `v`.
   118	
   119	There is no affine ramification: at every affine point of `C_L`, `F` identifies
   120	the tangent line to `C_L` with the tangent line to `L`. Finite branch values can
   121	therefore occur only where the cover is nonproper, namely the `n` transverse
   122	points of `L cap A_F`. The generic meridian cycle type is the one already used
   123	for MERIDIAN-FLOOR:
   124	
   125	```text
   126	1^a * product_l mu_l^{s_l},      W=N-a=sum_l s_l mu_l,      S=sum_l s_l.
   127	```
   128	
   129	This is MI:82-88 and DR:221-228. Over each of the `n` points of `L cap A_F`,
   130	the compactified fibre has `a` affine unramified points and `S` source-infinity
   131	places with ramification indices `mu_l` repeated `s_l` times. The ramification
   132	contribution is therefore
   133	
   134	```text
   135	sum_l s_l(mu_l-1) = W-S
   136	```
   137	
   138	per point. Over the target point `infty in P^1`, let `theta_inf` be the number
   139	of points of `X_L` in that fibre. The contribution over target infinity is
   140	`N-theta_inf`. Riemann-Hurwitz gives
   141	
   142	```text
   143	2g_L - 2 = -2N + n(W-S) + (N-theta_inf),
   144	```
   145	
   146	hence
   147	
   148	```text
   149	MF-EXACT:        n(W-S) = N - 2 + 2g_L + theta_inf.
   150	```
   151	
   152	The total number of source-infinity places of the plane curve `C_L` is
   153	
   154	```text
   155	theta_L = nS + theta_inf:
   156	```
   157	
   158	`nS` are over the finite points `L cap A_F`, and `theta_inf` are over target
   159	infinity. The Euler characteristic form is `chi(C_L)=N-nW`.
   160	
   161	The banked meridian floor follows from `g_L>=0` and `theta_inf>=1`. The exact
   162	defect is `2g_L+theta_inf-1`.
