    86	### 2.2 Proof A (block merge) — the banked argument, in one paragraph
    87	
    88	`F : A^2 \ E -> A^2 \ A_F` is a connected étale cover of degree `N`, so
    89	`rho : G -> S_N` is transitive. Under `H2` all meridians are conjugate, so each of
    90	the `n` generators has the generic cycle type `1^a · prod_l mu_l^{s_l}`
    91	(MI:694-695), i.e. `N - c(sigma) = W - S` with `W = N - a = sum_l s_l mu_l`,
    92	`S = sum_l s_l`. `N - c(sigma)` is the reflection length: adjoining one generator
    93	to a partition of the `N` sheets merges at most `W - S` blocks. Starting from `N`
    94	singletons and ending, by transitivity, at one block,
    95	
    96	```text
    97	        n (W - S)  >=  N - 1 ,      hence  n_min >= ceil((N-1)/(W-S)) >= ceil((N-1)/(W-1)).
    98	```
    99	
   100	### 2.3 Proof B (Riemann-Hurwitz) — and the floor becomes an identity
   101	
   102	Let `(u,v)` be generic affine coordinates on the target, `L := {u = c}` a generic
   103	line, `h := u∘F`, `h' := v∘F`, and `C_L := F^{-1}(L) = {h = c}`. (`u,v` are linear
   104	forms; the dicritical index `l` of `s_l, mu_l` is a different symbol and the two are
   105	never substituted.)
   106	
   107	* `F` is étale everywhere, so `dh = du ∘ dF` never vanishes: `C_L` is **smooth**,
   108	  `h - c` is reduced, and `deg C_L = D_F := max(deg P, deg Q)` for generic `u`.
   109	* `C_L \ E -> L \ A_F` is the restriction of the cover, étale of degree `N`, and
   110	  its monodromy is `rho ∘ (pi_1(L\A_F) ↠ G)`, hence transitive: **`C_L` is
   111	  connected**, so irreducible.
   112	* Let `X_L` be its smooth projective model. `F` followed by `L ≅ A^1 ⊂ P^1` gives
   113	  `pi : X_L -> P^1` of degree `N`, branched only over the `n` points of `L ∩ A_F`
   114	  and over `∞` (properness of `F` over `A^2 \ A_F` forbids any escaping branch
   115	  from converging to a point of `L \ A_F`).
   116	* Over `p_i ∈ L ∩ A_F` the fibre has `a + S` points: the `a` affine preimages,
   117	  unramified because `F` is a local biholomorphism there, and `S` places of `C_L`
   118	  at infinity carrying the ramification indices `mu_l` with multiplicity `s_l` —
   119	  which is Lemma 4.1's escaping count `N - a = W = sum_l s_l mu_l`, read on a
   120	  generic line. Ramification contribution `W - S` per point.
   121	* Over `∞` the fibre is `theta_inf` places, all at infinity of `C_L`.
   122	
   123	Riemann-Hurwitz `2g_L - 2 = -2N + n(W-S) + (N - theta_inf)` gives
   124	
   125	> **THEOREM MF-EXACT.** `n (W - S) = N - 2 + 2 g_L + theta_inf`, where `g_L` is the
   126	> genus and `theta_inf >= 1` the number of target-escaping places at infinity of
   127	> `C_L = F^{-1}(generic line)`. Equivalently `theta_L = nS + theta_inf` is the
   128	> total number of places of `C_L` at infinity, and `chi(C_L) = N - nW`.
   129	
   130	`g_L >= 0`, `theta_inf >= 1` re-prove MERIDIAN-FLOOR, and the identity names its
   131	**exact defect**: the floor is attained iff the generic fibre of a generic linear
   132	combination of `P,Q` is rational with a single target-escaping branch. This turns
   133	"sharpen the floor" into a concrete classical question about polynomial
   134	submersions `C^2 -> C` (`OPEN[MF-DEFECT]`, Sec 6).
